  "id": "paired-samples-t-test",
  "term": "paired-samples t test",
  "definition": "A paired-samples t test is a statistical test for two related measurements, such as scores from the same people under two conditions. It tests whether the difference scores between the paired measurements differ significantly from zero, making it mathematically equivalent to a one-sample t test on those differences.",
